      "text": "Aboulker, Bonnet, Picavet, and Trotignon prove NP-completeness for induced two-path routing even in a restricted class of string graphs. Their stronger flow theorem fixes two source terminals and two sink terminals. It does not automatically classify the language accepting all three perfect pairings.",
