      "text": "A local rulebook describes what a solution should look like near each node. Here a centralized program receives that rulebook and must decide whether random local decisions can coordinate a valid solution within a doubly logarithmic number of communication rounds. It is a question about automatically understanding algorithms, rather than running a particular algorithm on one tree."
